\chapter{Introduction and Motivation}
%===========================================================

The Computational Mucosal Dynamics (CMD) engine is a unified multi-scale
simulation architecture coupling astrophysical magnetohydrodynamic (MHD)
boundary fluxes, GPU-accelerated Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics (SPH),
viscoelastic PDE solvers, and immune tropical state-machine dynamics.
The objective is to construct a formally verified, cryptographically
anchored simulation manifold capable of reproducing complex biological
and astrophysical interactions with bit-exact determinism.

We motivate the CMD framework by demonstrating that biological mucosal
systems and astrophysical turbulence share structural invariants that
can be mapped via a scale-transformation functor $\mathcal{F}$.

